## 7. Lessons Learned

- Configuration profiles must have the correct assignment scope.
- Devices missing from an assigned group may not receive the intended policy.
- Intune synchronisation helps devices receive updated configurations.
- Individual settings can fail even when a profile has been assigned.
- Multiple configuration profiles can conflict when they configure the same setting differently.
- Administrators should establish the intended security configuration before resolving conflicts.
- Security policies should not be disabled simply to make deployment errors disappear.
- Always verify individual settings after remediation.

## 8. Ticket Closure

**Final Status:** Resolved

OPS-LAP-018 successfully received the required Windows security configuration. All three settings were confirmed as successful, and Thabo verified the expected screen-lock behaviour.

**Environment:** Simulated Microsoft 365 administration lab. No production tenant, real employee account or corporate device was accessed.

